before('Data availability',[P('The strengthening extension is reproduced from extensions/strengthening_20261015: acquire_external_data.py preserves sources; method_benchmark/run_method_benchmark.py and run_strengthened_methods.py rebuild nested predictions; run_matched_grid_comparator.py rebuilds the matched follow-up; correction_benchmark/run_count_benchmark.py --repetitions 100 rebuilds the 1,400 count datasets; biological_validation/prepare_external_metadata.py and run_biological_validation.py rebuild endpoint families. Independent verification scripts accompany each analysis. requirements_strengthening.txt and runtime_strengthening.txt record the extension environment separately from historical runs. For document generation, run scripts/build_strengthening_figures.py, integrate_strengthening.py, render_equations.cjs, refine_journal_artwork.cjs and build_final_documents.py, then render and validate both documents. Saved pre-extension content snapshots make integration repeatable without modifying the earlier sealed revision.')])
main[idx('Data availability')+1]['text']+=' The additional source accessions are OSD-202, OSD-352, OSD-374 and OSD-611 [35,36,37,38]. Their original acquired matrices, ISA archives, sample masks and membership provenance accompany the package. Full nested predictions, convex certificates, all 19,600 count-benchmark rows and the complete new biological family are included in numbered Supplementary Data and the extension directories.'
main[idx('Ethics statement')+1]['text']+=' The four additional deposits are also secondary public-data analyses; their original study ethics and husbandry records are retained with the ISA protocols. No new animal procedures were conducted for this extension.'
# A separately retained matched-grid comparison isolates tuning-grid differences.
before('The constrained algorithm generalizes to four external prediction settings',[
 P('A matched-grid follow-up then used the same baseline/10/1/0.1/0.01 candidates, identical preprocessing and nested folds for both ordinary and post-fit-clipped ridge across all 426 original/external holdouts. Constrained regression had lower equal-split/unit mean MSE than matched clipped ridge in every setting. The matched clipped ratios were 0.9896, 0.9628 and 0.9675 in the original settings and 0.9510, 0.9936, 0.9606 and 0.9738 externally. This improvement was not uniform: in OSD-611 only 3/10 individual pools favored the constrained estimator, and pooled SSE favored clipping (0.9809 versus 0.9836). Twenty-eight representative fixed-alpha checks independently confirmed lower training objectives for constrained fitting than clipping; this is distinct from a claim of uniformly better held-out prediction.')])
before('Gain constrained regression and exact operator geometry',[
 P('The matched-grid follow-up repeats ordinary and clipped ridge with exactly the five constrained candidates and the same preprocessing, nuisance design, outer roles and inner folds. Its 852 comparator rows and all paired differences are retained separately from the initial benchmark. Twenty-eight fixed-alpha first-split comparisons span seven datasets and four nonzero penalties. Coefficient reconstruction and full-space loss calculations independently verify the training-objective ordering. The reported mean, median, pooled-SSE and individual-unit comparisons are descriptive; no post hoc favorable weighting rule is substituted for the full results.')])
